==========================================================================
  VERDICT (delay, usage at 'both'): INCONCLUSIVE but directional, and NOT symmetric between the hypotheses. Neither coefficient clears alpha = 0.05 at n = 24 (df = 20). b_a = +0.0207 [-0.0214, +0.0628], p = 0.317 — point estimate runs AGAINST H1' (H1' predicts b_a < 0). b_s = -0.0886 [-0.2037, +0.0265], p = 0.124 — H2's direction. Largest standardised effect: control_deletion (beta* = +0.537). Availability remains flat (b_a p = 0.675), a third independent replication of it. Read as: H1' gained no support even with its confound removed, the residual signal is selectivity and general robustness, and the design is underpowered to separate a modest H2 effect from none.
  b_a at every site: l1 -0.0101 (p = 0.560), l2 +0.1365 (p = 0.000), both +0.0207 (p = 0.317)
  This grid moves both layers' activity together by construction, so every b_a above is a NETWORK-level coefficient (document 7 §6 point 1).
==========================================================================

